  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>20</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>56</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>90</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>140</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>112</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>120</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>60</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>14</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>7</mn></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mi>&#969;</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mi>&#969;</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math>&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;be the identity matrix of order <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>. If the determinant of the matrix <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> is equal to _________.<gwmw style=\"display:none;\"></gwmw>",
    "image": null
